{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser","id":607735,"title":"C20 Teaser","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-30T05:39:03-07:00","id":607735,"title":"C20 Teaser","content":"The 2015-2016 Onyx Path brochure is available! There's a nice teaser for Changeling's 20th Anniversary Edition:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/kQMUfLN.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The rest of the brochure is as <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/153331/Onyx-Path-20152016-Publishing-Brochure?affiliate_id=1362\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...iliate_id=1362</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T06:04:12-07:00","id":607757,"title":"","content":"This is awesome! Especially having the gallain in the core book. They should be better integrated in the setting this time around. I hope the Merfolk and Menehune will also be there although they're not explicitely mentioned.<br /> I can't wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T09:05:12-07:00","id":607958,"title":"","content":"O. M. G.<br /> <br /> This is SO exciting! I didn't think they'd include the hsien in the core book, so that's interesting.<br /> <br /> The description is just vague enough that we won't really know what's coming until they give us some more teasers. But I can live with that :P I guess it means stuff's still percolating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T10:48:16-07:00","id":608190,"title":"","content":"I'll straight up say it (again): I'm not a huge fan of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, but THIS is a product I'm proper chuffed to see!<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's something that I kept telling anyone who'd mention the game those same gripes: 'It ain't dark enough!' 'It's too limited in terms of kiths!' 'It just doesn't have enough possible scope!' However, the Twentieth Anniversary (...and for all intents and purposes long-awaited Revised Edition) <b>Changeling</b> shall address all of those gripes far better than, 'Look into the supplements,' that I heard before... And yesh, said supplements ARE great, so seeing that material integrated into the <b>Changeling 20</b> shall be fantastic!<br /> <br /> I can't wait to be proved WRONG about <b>Changeling</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:09:10-07:00","id":609814,"title":"","content":"Hsien in the core. That's... odd. I wonder how they will pull it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:20:46-07:00","id":609823,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://postcron.com/es/blog/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/MR-BURNS-EXCELLENT-1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> yes.....yes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:31:47-07:00","id":609875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=609814#post609814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hsien in the core. That's... odd. I wonder how they will pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that too. But, given the way nWoD works, perhaps OPP decided the easiest thing to do was have them use CTD's regular mechanics and then just bolt on a few extra traits? I kinda liked the hsien as they were, though, so I hope they don't change them too much by shaving off the serial numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:45:19-07:00","id":620950,"title":"","content":"The X20 series are tomes of information for the fat splats all crammed into one book, stripping out the metaplots, and cleaning up some rules just enough so that they are recognizable by players of all revisions, and yet updated for the modern setting (19 years after 2nd Edition!)<br /> <br /> V20 included long-dead lines, and bloodlines so obscure that some were only printed in low-circulation trade magazines, so it doesn't surprise me that they're including the Eastern groups, even if they do require some mechanical augmentations. ^.^<br /> <br /> With DriveThruCards, I also wouldn't be surprised if they offer new Cantrip cards either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T04:54:18-07:00","id":624083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=620950#post620950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The X20 series are tomes of information for the fat splats all crammed into one book, stripping out the metaplots, and cleaning up some rules just enough so that they are recognizable by players of all revisions, and yet updated for the modern setting (19 years after 2nd Edition!)<br /> <br /> V20 included long-dead lines, and bloodlines so obscure that some were only printed in low-circulation trade magazines, so it doesn't surprise me that they're including the Eastern groups, even if they do require some mechanical augmentations. ^.^<br /> <br /> With DriveThruCards, I also wouldn't be surprised if they offer new Cantrip cards either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> V20 didn't include KOTE stuff and honestly Hsien were probably less similar to Kithain than Kindred are to KOTE. Hell they had a magic system that would make a damned good set of pillars for a DA Mage Taoist faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T02:55:18-07:00","id":625268,"title":"","content":"V20 got so many power systems included, though, that I don't doubt they can fit in Hsien magic. There's less to cram in elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T02:44:01-07:00","id":626447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=625268#post625268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 got so many power systems included, though, that I don't doubt they can fit in Hsien magic. There's less to cram in elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are 27 Arts which is comparable to Discipline numbers, Realms adds greater diversity. Counting various kiths alone among the Kithain, Nunahei and Inanimae gives a splat number coming up on clans/bloodlines. The Dreaming itself should require some serious word count. Glamour, Banality the unique mechanics for Nunahei and Inanimae. adhere don't seem to be on the list, so that's probably cut out.<br /> <br /> Then You add in Hsien who don't use any of the mechanics of Kithain at all and have to add in new things.. unless the Hsien get a retcon(Gods know a Pooka is a better tanuki than Tanuki!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T11:17:04-07:00","id":626750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=626447#post626447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are 27 Arts which is comparable to Discipline numbers, Realms adds greater diversity. Counting various kiths alone among the Kithain, Nunahei and Inanimae gives a splat number coming up on clans/bloodlines. The Dreaming itself should require some serious word count. Glamour, Banality the unique mechanics for Nunahei and Inanimae. adhere don't seem to be on the list, so that's probably cut out.<br /> <br /> Then You add in Hsien who don't use any of the mechanics of Kithain at all and have to add in new things.. unless the Hsien get a retcon(Gods know a Pooka is a better tanuki than Tanuki!)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what happens when you mix up badgers and raccoon dogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:30:09-07:00","id":626814,"title":"","content":"The Disciplines often range from 1-9, while Arts range from 1-5. Even with the Realms thrown in, I can't see them taking up more space than V20's Disciplines. But even if they do, CTD has had much less published material than the Big Three games anyway, so that does leave space for things like Hsien. Although, I agree, it's an odd priority: Adhene would be more important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T18:12:45-07:00","id":627143,"title":"","content":"I don't think this has been posted around here yet. Matthew McFarland and Maggie Carroll were interviewed in a podcast: <a href=\"http://rickacarroll.com/podcast/episode-0012-smoot-presents-matt-mcfarland-and-maggie-carroll/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rickacarroll.com/podcast/epis...aggie-carroll/</a><br /> <br /> They talked briefly about C20 (starting at about the 29 minute mark) and revealed a few of the authors - Ian Lemke, Jackie Cassada, and Nicky Rae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T01:55:03-07:00","id":627378,"title":"","content":"I can't get the podcast to work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll try again on my laptop later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:43:17-07:00","id":628047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=624083#post624083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 didn't include KOTE stuff and honestly Hsien were probably less similar to Kithain than Kindred are to KOTE. Hell they had a magic system that would make a damned good set of pillars for a DA Mage Taoist faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which book(s) originally covered the <i>Hsien</i>? The &quot;little gods&quot; were mentioned in the <b>Kindred of the East</b> books, but I didn't realize they'd been developed that thoroughly (their own magic system?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T16:23:08-07:00","id":628103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=628047#post628047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book(s) originally covered the <i>Hsien</i>? The &quot;little gods&quot; were mentioned in the <b>Kindred of the East</b> books, but I didn't realize they'd been developed that thoroughly (their own magic system?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Land of Eight Million Dreams. They're literally divine servants who were trapped in the material world, in human bodies, rather than fae doing the same. Their magic system and kiths were based on the Daoist Wuxing (with Nei Dan, or internal alchemy, as a sixth category). Each of the Wuxing or Internal categories determines what you can do, like a Mage Sphere in some respects, with difficulty based on a character's attunement to Yin or Yang (effects were categorized as one of the two based on what they did, and dice pools would also vary based on this), and required successes based on the extent of the effect. You could get a boost up with traditional ritual behavior, such as wearing a corresponding color, standing in a certain direction relative to the subject/target, use of paper effigies, etc. It was rather neat, but also perhaps a bit narrowly focused on Daoism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T01:31:21-07:00","id":628371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=626814#post626814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Disciplines often range from 1-9, while Arts range from 1-5. Even with the Realms thrown in, I can't see them taking up more space than V20's Disciplines. But even if they do, CTD has had much less published material than the Big Three games anyway, so that does leave space for things like Hsien. Although, I agree, it's an odd priority: Adhene would be more important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the adhene won't be in the book, which... we don't know. The advert doesn't mention the Dauntain, and I'm doubtful they'd be left out of C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T15:09:47-07:00","id":629119,"title":"","content":"Im trying to contact Mr Gaiman for the possibility of a Foreword in C20, cross yer fingers guys","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T01:18:09-07:00","id":630793,"title":"","content":"Why can't there be hsien in core book? It would be just another big appendix, just like many others (Changing Breeds in W20?)<br /> <br /> I'd like them to rip the lore of from Keys to the Kingdom and other non-published material. There is huge reason why fans invented African, Middle-eastern (Asuras? Genies?) and Slavic changelings. Good Appendix is big appendix :&gt; Or just some hints about next splat book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T02:42:08-07:00","id":630887,"title":"","content":"You'd need 90-120 pages at least to give the Hsien any justice. And they are almost a thing of their own, as they barely use any other mechanics of other Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T04:02:29-07:00","id":630941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=630887#post630887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd need 90-120 pages at least to give the Hsien any justice. And they are almost a thing of their own, as they barely use any other mechanics of other Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>My suspicion ever since seeing the teaser has been that C20's Gallain will be handled like how the W20 core handled the Changing Breeds - an abbreviated form groups can use in their games, with perhaps an in-depth look coming down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T05:43:54-07:00","id":631072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=630941#post630941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My suspicion ever since seeing the teaser has been that C20's Gallain will be handled like how the W20 core handled the Changing Breeds - an abbreviated form groups can use in their games, with perhaps an in-depth look coming down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as they don't go the nWoD route of creating one character template which you just bolt new stats onto, I'll be happy. My worry is that the hsien will instead be portrayed as regular kith with a few tweaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T09:08:00-07:00","id":631249,"title":"","content":"Just some numbers boys <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It took pages from 364-472 (about hundred) on W20 to describe kinfolk, about 14 changing breeds, lost tribes, Pentex with all it's different agencies. Well, there were no gifts for changing breeds - cause they were invented rather as allies (gifts are suggested to take from different tribes which suits mostly). They had their own handbook. But it was very good to place changing breeds that simply (the way they were done so in Players Handbook in WTA) anyone can find them in core book and know them easily.<br /> <br /> It is nearly sure if there would be additional handbook for C20, these would be one with entire chapters about Hsien, Denizens, Dauntain, Thallain etc. And of course some new ones, cause this game was really vulnerable to add-onns and has many black spots on map of many continents. There should be summarized information about US Concordia and Isle of Mighty&amp;Emerald Isle (UK&amp;Ireland) and expanded another realms only mentioned in The Way of Commoner. I'm polish, but I'd also love to read about French sidhe-controlled lands and commoner-like eastern-darker Europe and some warmer Castillia (Spain) etc.I said that many times. <br /> <br /> And also - there would be much more space for WTO and CTD in these predicted 500 pages, because they aren't that huge splat lines. Just a history stuff, The Dreaming stuff, about 20 kiths and 15 noble houses, about 50 more other kiths, its okaaaaaaay :P Glamour systems were waiting for The Book of Glamour (another book that wasnt released along with The Keys to the Kingdom in Year of Scarab), so I'm prepared for some earthquakes in Arts &amp; Realms (and every change would be still awesome). But now I think that CTD was inspiration for Geist: The Sin-Eaters keys&amp;manifestations. One of most exciting mechanics imho.<br /> <br /> While Mage was about coincidence working, Changeling was always about good bunk. Imagination which was rewarded with best effects. That's the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:11:24-07:00","id":631320,"title":"","content":"TBH, 528pp for CTD is plenty (if it's the same length as V20). CTD 2e was 291pp, including the character sheet and index. That gives us 237pp to add in the extra kiths, the noble houses, the thallain, the gallain and the kinain, plus info on the Dreaming and additional Arts. That might just about work. The book can toss the introductions to RPGs because it's not an introductory book. And the old Glamour systems and rules will streamlined (and perhaps made more concise), so needn't necessarily eat into the page count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T14:05:59-07:00","id":631537,"title":"","content":"The idea that changeling some how has less to cover than Vampire is just ludicrous. Vampire doesn't have to cove a whole realm of existence and 3 layers of it. Glamour and Banality are a contentious and confusing topic(Just ask if it says &quot;science is bad&quot; or not) these are mechanics and setting bits that can use more word count not less.<br /> <br /> As for a cut down Hsien like the changeing breeds in werewolf.. they aren't like the changeing breeds in werewolf its not because they had theirown book we are saying this its like saying &quot;Mummy came out for Vampire intially lets have Mummy in the Vampire book&quot; that's how much mechanically they have in common with Kithain, they don't use glamour, or banality, or interact with the dreaming at all. I'd personally like to see them retconned back into Dreaming creatures but I don't know if they have the option to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:47:48-07:00","id":655872,"title":"","content":"Brief news from DragonCon: I asked Matt about how the hsien were being handled, and it involves the material from LO8MD being condensed and to be expanded upon in some fashion (stretch goals, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:31:05-07:00","id":656857,"title":"","content":"That's good to know. I think it'll be like Changing Breeds in Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T16:46:48-08:00","id":767428,"title":"","content":"From <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/shattered-smothered-covered-chunked-diced-peppered-capped-and-topped-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">today's Monday Meeting Notes</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Very pleased to say that we\u2019ve been OK\u2019d to go ahead with the <b>Changeling: the Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition</b> Kickstarter that we\u2019ve planned for December into January. This is, of course, the fifth of the Big Five gamelines, and we\u2019re thrilled to be creating an edition that celebrates our shared love of <b>CtD</b>! We\u2019ve got some great ideas for this one and I\u2019m going to run a few possible options past our printers this week. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T18:26:16-08:00","id":767497,"title":"","content":"ETERNAL WINTER IS COMING","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T02:07:50-08:00","id":767670,"title":"","content":"Can't wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T03:24:12-08:00","id":767711,"title":"","content":"Fantastic. Now they have to read all our threads of beg-content ^^<br /> <br /> I just wondered, if OnyxPath has so workers from WhiteWolf, so they have access to authentic material from unreleased Book of Glamour and Arabian Nights like Keys to the Kingdom?<br /> Just add along with Norse/Germanic also Slavic folklore and we are satisfied all along. (And Latin America and Africa and Far East.. and Oceania..)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:14:47-08:00","id":767753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=767711#post767711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fantastic. Now they have to read all our threads of beg-content</div> </div> </div> </div>I have it on good authority that at least one of the authors on C20 reads all of the Changeling related forum posts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T14:07:12-08:00","id":768087,"title":"","content":"C20 .... everything is going to be alright. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/571-nin","name":"Nin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T00:04:43-08:00","id":770570,"title":"","content":"I'm so looking forward to C20! I'm kind of new to the OP forums so does anyone know if any of the staff have directly engaged the members asking about what needs to be included in C20? I'd be interested in reading up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3583-wendell_burke","name":"Wendell_Burke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T04:43:44-08:00","id":770657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wendell_Burke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=770570#post770570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so looking forward to C20! I'm kind of new to the OP forums so does anyone know if any of the staff have directly engaged the members asking about what needs to be included in C20? I'd be interested in reading up.</div> </div> </div> </div>No-one on the writing team's asked on the forums about what needs to be included. Matt McFarland, C20's dev, has mentioned a couple of things he's planning to do, such as presenting the sidhe so they have some redeeming value to other fae and the modern world, and making changelings more magically impressive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T08:58:48-08:00","id":770764,"title":"","content":"So, here's a thing I kind of knew, but really got reinforced recently. Writers and other creative folks are extremely interested in the discussions, but can't really participate a lot of times. This might be due to non-disclosure agreements. It might be because they've already got something done and fans come up with something similar. They don't want anyone to think their ideas are being stolen.<br /> <br /> One thing's for sure though - everyone on the various OPP creative teams are all hardcore fans themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T09:48:11-08:00","id":770804,"title":"","content":"I hope Arts get reworked so that each level can be used with every Realm. The problem I see is that some Realms get used a lot more than others, and some cantrips only use one or two Realms at most. Allowing for creative uses of Arts and Realms would be a big help in making magic more versatile. For example, how might you use Fugue with the Prop Realm? Or Sovereign with Prop? These combinations should be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T08:46:51-08:00","id":772339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=770657#post770657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No-one on the writing team's asked on the forums about what needs to be included. Matt McFarland, C20's dev, has mentioned a couple of things he's planning to do, such as presenting the sidhe so they have some redeeming value to other fae and the modern world, and making changelings more magically impressive</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm paying attention, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T09:08:45-08:00","id":772352,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see Leif Jones and Brian LeBlanc back for art duties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T09:51:31-08:00","id":772379,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they have the budget to get DiTerlizzi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:25:19-08:00","id":772691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=772339#post772339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm paying attention, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I will repost my suggestion to change the Chu-ih-yu to Ch'ih-yu; -ih denotes an empty rime sound, where you extend the initial syllable, in this case an aspirated ch as in chart, and yu in Wade-Giles is pronounced like the English greeting &quot;yo&quot;. Or, if we can change everything to hanyu pinyin that people can type into Google translate, Chiyou. I think a lack of experience with aspiration marks back during writing may have caused a typo, since all the other references to figures of the Three Sovereigns and Five Emperors era were correctly Romanized for Wade-Giles, minus the tones of course. Also, there's that one KotE Discipline that's supposed to be Ch'ih-mu but got butchered horribly into Chi'iu Muh. Extra vowels seemed to be a problem at least one other time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:52:12-08:00","id":772710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=772339#post772339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm paying attention, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> good to know... and good luck\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9055-gmforpowergamers","name":"Gmforpowergamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T16:13:25-08:00","id":775085,"title":"","content":"If we're gonna talk about artists I <b>need</b> Rebecca Guay &amp; Mark Jackson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T06:24:07-08:00","id":775425,"title":"","content":"Mark Jackson's work on Changeling was amazing! I'm not sure if he does RPG art anymore though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T13:48:38-08:00","id":775614,"title":"","content":"Hsien bother me a lot. I think they are really cool, but are a bad fit IMO, for changelings. As gods exiled to creation they always made a better fit in my mind for a Eastern equivalent of Demon the Fallen than Changeling, since the Elohim are basically all the godlings from the Mesopotamian pantheons who got demoted after Yahweh was made the &quot;Only True God&quot; when the Torah was edited. Making the splat that used the Hsien rules an equivalent to the Elohim freed me to use the basic changeling rules for statting the creatures in Lo8MD that did conform to what i thought of as Fair Folk. I borrowed bits and pieces from Scion and wikipedia to fill in the gaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T15:31:54-08:00","id":775662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=775614#post775614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hsien bother me a lot. I think they are really cool, but are a bad fit IMO, for changelings. As gods exiled to creation they always made a better fit in my mind for a Eastern equivalent of Demon the Fallen than Changeling, since the Elohim are basically all the godlings from the Mesopotamian pantheons who got demoted after Yahweh was made the &quot;Only True God&quot; when the Torah was edited. Making the splat that used the Hsien rules an equivalent to the Elohim freed me to use the basic changeling rules for statting the creatures in Lo8MD that did conform to what i thought of as Fair Folk. I borrowed bits and pieces from Scion and wikipedia to fill in the gaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could also go the other way and just toss Demon in as a subdirectory of Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T21:43:40-08:00","id":775795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=775614#post775614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hsien bother me a lot. I think they are really cool, but are a bad fit IMO, for changelings. As gods exiled to creation they always made a better fit in my mind for a Eastern equivalent of Demon the Fallen than Changeling, since the Elohim are basically all the godlings from the Mesopotamian pantheons who got demoted after Yahweh was made the &quot;Only True God&quot; when the Torah was edited. Making the splat that used the Hsien rules an equivalent to the Elohim freed me to use the basic changeling rules for statting the creatures in Lo8MD that did conform to what i thought of as Fair Folk. I borrowed bits and pieces from Scion and wikipedia to fill in the gaps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which did you pick were still gods and which did you feel were proper fae? The HIrayanu in my mind work out to be hitting many of the creatures that are Faeish in myths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:45:28-08:00","id":776150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=775662#post775662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One could also go the other way and just toss Demon in as a subdirectory of Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Thats hilarious and true. I prefer to keep Exalted in mind in my head canon tho. That means nothing to the CWoD canon, but it does inform my preferences. Changelings descend from Raksha, and Demons, and Hsien/godlings/etc trace descent from the gods of Exalted, for me anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:54:07-08:00","id":776157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=776150#post776150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha! Thats hilarious and true. I prefer to keep Exalted in mind in my head canon tho. That means nothing to the CWoD canon, but it does inform my preferences. Changelings descend from Raksha, and Demons, and Hsien/godlings/etc trace descent from the gods of Exalted, for me anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel Fallen Demons fit the whole Exalted Paradigm at all, on the other hand if they are Fairies playing a role...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:56:44-08:00","id":776159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=775795#post775795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Which did you pick were still gods and which did you feel were proper fae? The HIrayanu in my mind work out to be hitting many of the creatures that are Faeish in myths</div> </div> </div> </div>T<br /> <br /> Thats true, and thats where it gets complicated for me. I effectively yoinked the Hsien rules to use for KotE Demon spalt equivalent, who i called the Shinma, and left the Hsien as a Dreaming connected Changeling equivalent splat.<br /> <br /> To further define the Shinma, i borrowed heavily from Scion as i said, but also my one of my favourite novels Barry Hughart's &quot;Bridge Of Birds&quot;.<br /> So i ended up with a global splat of exiled divinities who reap Faith, who are defined by local paradigm,They use Lores if they dwell in lands where the Abrahamic faiths are strong, but use the Hsien rules in the Eastern WoD.<br /> <br /> Then i as a consequence had a global splat connected to the Dreaming who appear as the spirits of nature and the Wyld who reap Glamour in the west and Yang Chi/Yugen in the East<br /> <br /> This was just so i could have one Hsien npc who my Demon player encountered and mess with her head when he pointed out that they were the same thing just filtered thru different local paradigms. And drop clues about the time the world was flat and they served the Celestines in Yu Shan. Totally worth it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:06:36-08:00","id":776161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=776157#post776157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't feel Fallen Demons fit the whole Exalted Paradigm at all, on the other hand if they are Fairies playing a role...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally understand that, but for my head canon, the Fallen, and the Hsien are the Pure Ones who are referred to in Shifter mythology iirc? The beings who existed before the Breaking, and in my head canon i assigned them as the gods of exalted, in keeping with each Exaled splat having a CWoD equivalent/descendant. The specific gods i assigned were the Ascended dead who served the Unconquered Sun who appear in the Daystar stuff. But again, my head canon only.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:41:04-08:00","id":776355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607735-c20-teaser?p=776150#post776150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha! Thats hilarious and true. I prefer to keep Exalted in mind in my head canon tho. That means nothing to the CWoD canon, but it does inform my preferences. Changelings descend from Raksha, and Demons, and Hsien/godlings/etc trace descent from the gods of Exalted, for me anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons and Fair Folk were never really closely related, though; there was that line of conjecture about Primordials being some kind of Fair Folk that changed itself due to how the soul structures shook out and how some raksha could put their Graces in other fae, but it wasn't something that was really strongly supported, except in character by raksha, so it wasn't really a thing to be trusted. Besides, if you group the kithain and shinma together with the Inanimae, you cover all three non-ghost spirit types from classic Exalted!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T18:52:03-08:00","id":795290,"title":"","content":"I wrote up a summary of my first actual playtest session of C20. Matt asked me to link to it on the Kickstarter, so I figured folks here would be interested too. I'm posting the link in this thread because there are mentions of a few things that haven't been revealed elsewhere yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/charlie-cantrell/c20-playtest-recap/10153514986829635\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/rsrc.php/y8/r/dF5SId3UHWd.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/charlie-cantrell/c20-playtest-recap/10153514986829635\" target=\"_blank\"> Log into Facebook </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/charlie-cantrell/c20-playtest-recap/10153514986829635\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.facebook.com/notes/charlie-cantrell/c20-playtest-recap/10153514986829635 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Log into Facebook to start sharing and connecting with your friends, family, and people you know. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I had so much fun running the game! I hope others enjoy reading it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight